	(text_box "Values and why (ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 datasheet v1.8 section 9; Espressif ESP32-S3 hardware design guidelines)\n- Module supply: 22 uF + 100 nF at the 3V3 pin, as in Espressif's peripheral schematic.\n- EN: R205 47k to +3V3 and C203 220 nF release EN with 47k x 220 nF = 10.3 ms (Espressif: 10k x 1 uF = 10 ms).\n  TPS63802 PG (open drain, TPS_PG, specified to sink up to 1 mA) holds EN low through R212 4.7k until 3.3 V is above\n  95 % and pulls it low below 90 %. PG then sinks at most 3.3 V / 4.7k = 0.70 mA (0.63 mA at the 90 % trip), and the\n  47k / 4.7k divider holds EN at 0.30 V or less (VIL_nRST max 0.25 x VDD = 0.74 V at 2.97 V). EN falls with\n  (47k || 4.7k) x 220 nF = 0.94 ms, which filters PG glitches shorter than about 1 ms. TP201 to GND resets the module.\n- Straps at reset: GPIO0 (BOOT) 10k pull-up = SPI boot; short TP202 to TP203 during reset for download mode.\n  GPIO45 (CHG_SUSPEND) and GPIO46 (DISP_EN) have 100k pull-downs on the power sheet (VDD_SPI 3.3 V, SPI boot).\n  GPIO3 (BTN_EAR_R) is a strap only once the JTAG eFuse is burned; its 100k pull-up keeps it high anyway.\n- Crystal Q13FC13500004: CL 12.5 pF, ESR 70k max (Espressif asks for 70k or less), +-20 ppm.\n  C = 2 x (CL - Cstray) = 2 x (12.5 - 3.5) = 18 pF. Measure the RTC drift at bring-up; adjust C204/C205 above 20 ppm.\n- USB: native USB Serial/JTAG on GPIO19/20, full speed. USBLC6-2SC6 at the connector, 22 ohm series resistors next\n  to the module (Espressif: reserve 22 to 33 ohm). CC1 and CC2 each have their own 5.1k Rd (sink, 5 V only).\n  Both D+ pins (A6, B6) and both D- pins (A7, B7) are joined; SBU open; shell to GND.\n- VBUS_USB has only the SMF5.0A TVS here, no capacitor: a USB host sees C101 4.7 uF behind D101 (power sheet), within\n  USB's 10 uF. U202 pin 5 (VBUS) is left open, so the ESP32-S3's D+ pull-up cannot back-feed the receptacle's VBUS\n  through the upper steering diode while unplugged; the ESD clamp works without it.\n- Buttons: switch to GND, 100k to +3V3, 10 nF (1 ms). External pull-ups let ext1 ANY_LOW wake work with the RTC\n  peripherals off; every wake pin is an RTC GPIO (0 to 21).\n- J202 follows the Qwiic order (GND, 3V3, SDA, SCL): an EC11 encoder (A and B switch to GND) or an I2C test device.\n- UART0 (GPIO43 TX, GPIO44 RX) reaches only pads TP204 and TP205, for a 3.3 V serial adapter. Espressif's 499 ohm\n  U0TXD series resistor is inside the module (WROOM-1 datasheet figure 8-1, R3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
